        "jiutangshu:129:p017"
      ],
      "anchorLocalId": "jiutangshu:129:p017",
      "ownerFinding": "Unnamed inferred placeholder, and its single-daughter model is also unsupported. s0037 「兩婿先已當辜，趙縱今又下獄」 and s0038 「連罪三婿」 refer to Guo Ziyi's three sons-in-law (Zhao Zong being the third), which implies several daughters; none is named or quoted anywhere in the chapter. The extraction itself records \"no non-overlapping surface names her\". Zhao Zong's son-in-law link to Guo Ziyi (claim 160, explicit) stands without an intermediary. Remove p017; keep claim 160 without intermediaryPersonIds.",
      "ownerDisposition": "accept-hold-propose-remove-inferred-person",
      "independentVerdict": "hold",
      "primaryWitnessUnits": [
        {
          "unitId": "s0037",
          "path": "data/jiutangshu/129.json",
          "zh": "歿身未幾，墳土僅乾，兩婿先已當辜，趙縱今又下獄。",
          "enLiteral": "Not long after his death, the grave earth had barely dried; two sons-in-law had already been found guilty, and now Zhao Zong is again sent to prison.",
          "enIdiomatic": "Not long after his death, the earth on his grave had barely dried. Two sons-in-law had already been found guilty, and now Zhao Zong has been sent to prison as well."
        },
        {
          "unitId": "s0038",
          "path": "data/jiutangshu/129.json",
          "zh": "設令縱實抵法，所告非奴，才經數月，連罪三婿。",
          "enLiteral": "Even if Zong truly merited punishment under law, the accuser was not a slave, and within only a few months three sons-in-law have been punished in succession.",
          "enIdiomatic": "Even if Zhao Zong truly merited punishment under the law, the accuser was not a slave, and within only a few months three sons-in-law have been punished in succession."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "caseId": "sha256:d77e31aec651b9b661d99e6e5a1452237bc6124bf3d52ce70b4ebde680b4070a",
      "localId": "jiutangshu:129:p053",
      "canonicalPersonId": "per_PS982BWA1GZQ6DE99MA4",
      "transportLocalPeople": [
        "jiutangshu:129:p053"
      ],
      "protectedLocalPeople": [
        "jiutangshu:129:p053"
      ],
      "anchorLocalId": "jiutangshu:129:p053",
      "ownerFinding": "Unnamed inferred genealogical intermediary with no Chinese name at all (preferred zh null). s0098 「林甫之玄孫」, s0099 「祖令植」 and s0113 「祥道即從一曾伯祖也」 entail that Congyi's great-grandfather was a son of Lin Fu and a brother of Xiangdao, but no unit names or quotes him; the label 從一曾祖 is constructed. Outside knowledge of his name may not be imported. The explicit chain survives without him: p051 descendant-of p052 (玄孫, gen 4, claim 470), p054 ancestor-of p051 (祖, claim 531), p060 child-of p052 (claim 568), and p051 kin-of p060 (曾伯祖, claim 475). Remove p053; keep claim 475 without intermediaryPersonIds.",
      "ownerDisposition": "accept-hold-propose-remove-inferred-person",
      "independentVerdict": "hold",
      "primaryWitnessUnits": [
        {
          "unitId": "s0098",
          "path": "data/jiutangshu/129.json",
          "zh": "劉從一，中書侍郎林甫之玄孫也。",
          "enLiteral": "Liu Congyi was the great-great-grandson of Vice Director of the Secretariat Lin Fu.",
          "enIdiomatic": "Liu Congyi was the great-great-grandson of Vice Director of the Secretariat Lin Fu."
        },
        {
          "unitId": "s0099",
          "path": "data/jiutangshu/129.json",
          "zh": "祖令植，禮部侍郎。",
          "enLiteral": "His grandfather Lingzhi was vice minister of the Ministry of Rites.",
          "enIdiomatic": "His grandfather Lingzhi was vice minister of the Ministry of Rites."
        },
        {
          "unitId": "s0113",
          "path": "data/jiutangshu/129.json",
          "zh": "初，林甫生祥道，麟德初為右相，祥道即從一曾伯祖也。",
          "enLiteral": "At first, Lin Fu begot Xiangdao, who in the beginning of Linde served as right chief minister; Xiangdao was Congyi's great-granduncle.",
          "enIdiomatic": "Lin Fu's son Xiangdao served as right chief minister at the beginning of the Linde era; Xiangdao was Congyi's great-granduncle."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
